{
  "schema": 1,
  "id": "pim.data-models",
  "name": "One data model per top group, with its category, spec fields, display group and completeness rule",
  "functions": ["pim.data-models", "pim.field-scope", "pim.field-display-groups", "pim.completeness-rules"],
  "skill": "dw-demo-pim",
  "inputs": {"section": "catalogue", "required": ["groups", "pimFolder"]},
  "modes": {
    "mcpOnly": {"usable": false, "reason": "No MCP read lists a product category that has no fields yet (get_product_category_fields lists fields), so the category step needs the Management API read ProductCategoriesAll."},
    "hosted": {"usable": true, "reason": "Every step finds, writes and reads back with MCP tools and the Management API; nothing needs SQL or a recycle."},
    "local": {"usable": true},
    "layerDelivered": "verify"
  },
  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "folder",
      "title": "Ensure the data-model folder under the PIM shop by name",
      "key": "{input.pimFolder}",
      "find": {"bindings": [
        {"id": "mcp-shops", "surface": "mcp", "status": "implemented", "operation": "get_shops", "arguments": {"includeGroupHierarchy": true}, "rows": "data[*].dataModels", "match": {"name": "{input.pimFolder}"}, "produces": {"id": "id"}, "source": "skills/dw-pim-modelling/references/model-writes.md"}
      ]},
      "bindings": [
        {"id": "mcp-create-folder", "surface": "mcp", "status": "implemented", "source": "skills/dw-pim-modelling/references/model-writes.md",
          "create": {"operation": "create_data_models", "arguments": {"requests": [{"parentId": "{build.pimShop}", "model": {"name": "{input.pimFolder}", "type": "DataModelFolder"}}]}},
          "readBack": {"surface": "mcp", "status": "implemented", "operation": "get_shops", "arguments": {"includeGroupHierarchy": true}, "rows": "data[*].dataModels", "match": {"name": "{input.pimFolder}"}, "produces": {"id": "id"}, "source": "skills/dw-pim-modelling/references/model-writes.md"}}
      ],
      "trap": "get_shops nests the hierarchy: a folder sits in a shop's dataModels with its models in its own dataModels, while a model created straight under the shop is listed in topLevelDataModels instead.",
      "source": "skills/dw-pim-modelling/references/model-writes.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "categories",
      "title": "Ensure one CategoryFields product category per top group by name",
      "forEach": "groups[*]",
      "key": "{item.key}",
      "skipWhen": {"path": "item.parent", "exists": true},
      "find": {"bindings": [
        {"id": "mcp-categories", "surface": "mcp", "status": "planned", "reason": "No MCP read lists a category: get_product_category_fields returns the fields of CategoryFields categories, so a category without fields is invisible to it.", "source": "skills/dw-pim-modelling/references/model-writes.md"},
        {"id": "admin-categories", "surface": "admin-api", "status": "implemented", "operation": "ProductCategoriesAll", "arguments": {}, "rows": "model.data", "match": {"name": "{item.name}"}, "produces": {"id": "id"}, "source": "skills/dw-data-access/references/recipes-pim.md"}
      ]},
      "bindings": [
        {"id": "mcp-create-category", "surface": "mcp", "status": "implemented", "source": "skills/dw-pim-modelling/references/model-writes.md",
          "create": {"operation": "create_categories", "arguments": {"requests": [{"systemName": "{item.key}", "name": "{item.name}", "categoryType": "CategoryFields"}]}},
          "readBack": {"surface": "admin-api", "status": "implemented", "operation": "ProductCategoriesAll", "arguments": {}, "rows": "model.data", "match": {"name": "{item.name}"}, "produces": {"id": "id"}, "source": "skills/dw-data-access/references/recipes-pim.md"}}
      ],
      "trap": "create_categories drops the hyphens of a system name (my-tools becomes mytools) and answers isNew false even for a new category, so the category is found by name and its id is read back, never derived from the key.",
      "source": "skills/dw-pim-modelling/references/model-writes.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "models",
      "title": "Ensure one data model per top group in the folder, bound to its category",
      "forEach": "groups[*]",
      "key": "{item.key}",
      "skipWhen": {"path": "item.parent", "exists": true},
      "find": {"bindings": [
        {"id": "mcp-shops", "surface": "mcp", "status": "implemented", "operation": "get_shops", "arguments": {"includeGroupHierarchy": true}, "rows": "data[*].dataModels[*].dataModels", "match": {"name": "{item.name}"}, "compare": {"categoryId": "{step.categories.id}"}, "produces": {"id": "id"}, "source": "skills/dw-pim-modelling/references/model-writes.md"}
      ]},
      "bindings": [
        {"id": "mcp-model", "surface": "mcp", "status": "implemented", "source": "skills/dw-pim-modelling/references/model-writes.md",
          "create": {"operation": "create_data_models", "arguments": {"requests": [{"parentId": "{step.folder[input.pimFolder].id}", "model": {"name": "{item.name}", "type": "DataModel"}, "categoryId": "{step.categories.id}"}]}},
          "update": {"operation": "patch_data_models", "arguments": {"requests": [{"dataModelId": "{found.id}", "patch": {"categoryId": "{step.categories.id}"}}]}},
          "readBack": {"surface": "mcp", "status": "implemented", "operation": "get_shops", "arguments": {"includeGroupHierarchy": true}, "rows": "data[*].dataModels[*].dataModels", "match": {"name": "{item.name}"}, "expect": {"categoryId": "{step.categories.id}"}, "produces": {"id": "id"}, "source": "skills/dw-pim-modelling/references/model-writes.md"}}
      ],
      "trap": "create_data_models stores any categoryId, also one no category has, so the category step runs first and its read-back id is the one bound. Never bind a category through the Management API DataModelGroupSave with a partial model: it is a whole-entity save and clears the category.",
      "source": "skills/dw-pim-modelling/references/model-writes.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "fields",
      "title": "Ensure each spec field in its top group's category, the same in every language and variant",
      "forEach": "groups[*].specFields[*]",
      "key": "{parent.key}/{item.key}",
      "find": {"bindings": [
        {"id": "mcp-fields", "surface": "mcp", "status": "implemented", "operation": "get_product_category_fields", "arguments": {}, "rows": "data", "match": {"systemName": "ProductCategory|{step.categories[parent.key].id}|{item.key}"}, "compare": {"allowChangesAcrossLanguages": false, "allowChangesAcrossVariants": false}, "source": "skills/dw-pim-modelling/references/model-writes.md"}
      ]},
      "bindings": [
        {"id": "mcp-field", "surface": "mcp", "status": "implemented", "source": "skills/dw-pim-modelling/references/model-writes.md",
          "create": {"operation": "create_category_fields", "arguments": {"requests": [{"categoryId": "{step.categories[parent.key].id}", "fieldModel": {"id": "{item.key}", "label": "{item.label}", "templateTag": "{item.key}", "type": 1, "allowChangesAcrossLanguages": false, "allowChangesAcrossVariants": false}}]}},
          "update": {"operation": "update_category_fields", "arguments": {"requests": [{"categoryId": "{step.categories[parent.key].id}", "fieldId": "{item.key}", "allowChangesAcrossLanguages": false, "allowChangesAcrossVariants": false}]}},
          "readBack": {"surface": "mcp", "status": "implemented", "operation": "get_product_category_fields", "arguments": {}, "rows": "data", "match": {"systemName": "ProductCategory|{step.categories[parent.key].id}|{item.key}"}, "expect": {"label": "{item.label}", "allowChangesAcrossLanguages": false, "allowChangesAcrossVariants": false}, "source": "skills/dw-pim-modelling/references/model-writes.md"}}
      ],
      "trap": "Spec fields are Text (255), type 1. get_product_category_fields lists only CategoryFields categories, leaves fieldId empty and carries the id in systemName ProductCategory|<category>|<field>. update_category_fields sets the scope flags and not the label, so a changed label is not updated.",
      "source": "skills/dw-pim-modelling/references/model-writes.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "display-group",
      "title": "Ensure one storefront display group per top group holding its spec fields in input order",
      "forEach": "groups[*]",
      "key": "{item.key}",
      "skipWhen": {"path": "item.specFields", "exists": false},
      "find": {"bindings": [
        {"id": "mcp-display-groups", "surface": "mcp", "status": "implemented", "operation": "get_field_display_groups", "arguments": {}, "rows": "data", "match": {"systemName": "{step.categories.id}"}, "compare": {"name": "{item.name}", "availableInFrontend": true, "fieldIdsList": "ProductCategory|{step.categories.id}|{item.specFields[*].key}"}, "produces": {"id": "id"}, "source": "skills/dw-pim-modelling/references/model-writes.md"}
      ]},
      "bindings": [
        {"id": "mcp-display-group", "surface": "mcp", "status": "implemented", "source": "skills/dw-pim-modelling/references/model-writes.md",
          "create": {"operation": "save_field_display_group", "arguments": {"group": {"id": 0, "systemName": "{step.categories.id}", "name": "{item.name}", "availableInFrontend": true, "fieldIdsList": "ProductCategory|{step.categories.id}|{item.specFields[*].key}"}}},
          "update": {"operation": "save_field_display_group", "arguments": {"group": {"id": "{found.id}", "name": "{item.name}", "availableInFrontend": true, "fieldIdsList": "ProductCategory|{step.categories.id}|{item.specFields[*].key}"}}},
          "readBack": {"surface": "mcp", "status": "implemented", "operation": "get_field_display_groups", "arguments": {}, "rows": "data", "match": {"systemName": "{step.categories.id}"}, "expect": {"name": "{item.name}", "availableInFrontend": true, "fieldIdsList": "ProductCategory|{step.categories.id}|{item.specFields[*].key}"}, "produces": {"id": "id"}, "source": "skills/dw-pim-modelling/references/model-writes.md"}}
      ],
      "trap": "save_field_display_group takes one group object, not a list; id 0 creates and then needs a system name no other group has. fieldIdsList replaces the whole membership. The delivery API shows a display group on a product only while the product has a value in one of its fields.",
      "source": "skills/dw-pim-modelling/references/model-writes.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "rule",
      "title": "Ensure one completeness rule per top group over its spec fields",
      "forEach": "groups[*]",
      "key": "{item.key}",
      "skipWhen": {"path": "item.specFields", "exists": false},
      "find": {"bindings": [
        {"id": "mcp-rules", "surface": "mcp", "status": "implemented", "requiresSchema": {"output": ["data[*].fields"]}, "operation": "get_completion_rules", "arguments": {}, "rows": "data", "match": {"name": "{item.name} complete"}, "compare": {"excludeVariants": true, "fields[*].systemName": "ProductCategory|{step.categories.id}|{item.specFields[*].key}"}, "produces": {"id": "id"}, "source": "skills/dw-pim-completeness/references/rules-and-dashboards.md"},
        {"id": "mcp-rules-names", "surface": "mcp", "status": "implemented", "operation": "get_completion_rules", "arguments": {}, "rows": "data", "match": {"name": "{item.name} complete"}, "compare": {"excludeVariants": true, "fieldSystemNames": "ProductCategory|{step.categories.id}|{item.specFields[*].key}"}, "produces": {"id": "id"}, "source": "skills/dw-pim-completeness/references/rules-and-dashboards.md"}
      ]},
      "bindings": [
        {"id": "mcp-rule", "surface": "mcp", "status": "implemented", "source": "skills/dw-pim-completeness/references/rules-and-dashboards.md",
          "create": {"operation": "create_or_update_completeness_rules", "arguments": {"models": [{"id": 0, "name": "{item.name} complete", "excludeVariants": true, "fieldSystemNames": "ProductCategory|{step.categories.id}|{item.specFields[*].key}"}]}},
          "update": {"operation": "create_or_update_completeness_rules", "arguments": {"models": [{"id": "{found.id}", "name": "{item.name} complete", "excludeVariants": true, "fieldSystemNames": "ProductCategory|{step.categories.id}|{item.specFields[*].key}"}]}},
          "readBack": {"surface": "mcp", "status": "implemented", "requiresSchema": {"output": ["data[*].fields"]}, "operation": "get_completion_rules", "arguments": {}, "rows": "data", "match": {"name": "{item.name} complete"}, "expect": {"excludeVariants": true, "fields[*].systemName": "ProductCategory|{step.categories.id}|{item.specFields[*].key}"}, "produces": {"id": "id"}, "source": "skills/dw-pim-completeness/references/rules-and-dashboards.md"}},
        {"id": "mcp-rule-names", "surface": "mcp", "status": "implemented", "source": "skills/dw-pim-completeness/references/rules-and-dashboards.md",
          "create": {"operation": "create_or_update_completeness_rules", "arguments": {"models": [{"id": 0, "name": "{item.name} complete", "excludeVariants": true, "fieldSystemNames": "ProductCategory|{step.categories.id}|{item.specFields[*].key}"}]}},
          "update": {"operation": "create_or_update_completeness_rules", "arguments": {"models": [{"id": "{found.id}", "name": "{item.name} complete", "excludeVariants": true, "fieldSystemNames": "ProductCategory|{step.categories.id}|{item.specFields[*].key}"}]}},
          "readBack": {"surface": "mcp", "status": "implemented", "operation": "get_completion_rules", "arguments": {}, "rows": "data", "match": {"name": "{item.name} complete"}, "expect": {"excludeVariants": true, "fieldSystemNames": "ProductCategory|{step.categories.id}|{item.specFields[*].key}"}, "produces": {"id": "id"}, "source": "skills/dw-pim-completeness/references/rules-and-dashboards.md"}}
      ],
      "trap": "The rule read changed shape between server releases: up to 0.6.3 get_completion_rules returns each rule's fields as objects (fields[].systemName); from 0.6.6 its rows carry only the fieldSystemNames list the write takes. Each read is gated on the tools/list output schema listing fields[] (requiresSchema), so a server without it takes the fieldSystemNames binding.",
      "source": "skills/dw-pim-completeness/references/rules-and-dashboards.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "rule-assignment",
      "title": "Assign the rule to its data model in the default language",
      "forEach": "groups[*]",
      "key": "{item.key}",
      "skipWhen": {"path": "item.specFields", "exists": false},
      "find": {"bindings": [
        {"id": "mcp-assignments", "surface": "mcp", "status": "implemented", "operation": "get_completion_rule_assignments_for_groups", "arguments": {"groupIds": ["{step.models.id}"]}, "rows": "data", "match": {"id": "{step.models.id}"}, "compare": {"rules[*].ruleId": ["{step.rule.id}"], "languageIds": ["{build.defaultLanguage}"]}, "source": "skills/dw-pim-completeness/references/rules-and-dashboards.md"}
      ]},
      "bindings": [
        {"id": "mcp-assign", "surface": "mcp", "status": "implemented", "source": "skills/dw-pim-completeness/references/rules-and-dashboards.md",
          "create": {"operation": "assign_completion_rules_to_groups", "arguments": {"requests": [{"groupId": "{step.models.id}", "ruleIds": ["{step.rule.id}"], "languageIds": ["{build.defaultLanguage}"]}]}},
          "update": {"operation": "assign_completion_rules_to_groups", "arguments": {"requests": [{"groupId": "{step.models.id}", "ruleIds": ["{step.rule.id}"], "languageIds": ["{build.defaultLanguage}"]}]}},
          "readBack": {"surface": "mcp", "status": "implemented", "operation": "get_completion_rule_assignments_for_groups", "arguments": {"groupIds": ["{step.models.id}"]}, "rows": "data", "match": {"id": "{step.models.id}"}, "expect": {"rules[*].ruleId": ["{step.rule.id}"], "languageIds": ["{build.defaultLanguage}"]}, "source": "skills/dw-pim-completeness/references/rules-and-dashboards.md"}}
      ],
      "trap": "assign_completion_rules_to_groups replaces the group's whole assignment: a rule another recipe assigned to the same data model is removed.",
      "source": "skills/dw-pim-completeness/references/rules-and-dashboards.md"
    }
  ],
  "debts": [],
  "verify": {
    "checkIds": ["pim.data-models.folder", "pim.field-scope.declared-scope", "pim.field-display-groups.groups", "pim.field-display-groups.unnamed-groups", "pim.completeness-rules.rules", "pim.completeness-rules.models-without-rule"],
    "probes": [
      {
        "id": "model-unique",
        "title": "Each top group has exactly one data model of its name",
        "forEach": "groups[*]",
        "skipWhen": {"path": "item.parent", "exists": true},
        "minimumSubjects": 1,
        "bindings": [
          {"surface": "mcp", "status": "implemented", "operation": "get_shops", "arguments": {"includeGroupHierarchy": true}, "rows": "data[*].dataModels[*].dataModels", "match": {"name": "{item.name}"}, "assert": {"kind": "count", "op": "eq", "value": 1}, "source": "skills/dw-pim-modelling/references/model-writes.md"}
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "display-group-storefront",
        "title": "Each top group's display group is offered to the storefront",
        "forEach": "groups[*]",
        "skipWhen": {"path": "item.specFields", "exists": false},
        "minimumSubjects": 1,
        "bindings": [
          {"surface": "mcp", "status": "implemented", "operation": "get_field_display_groups", "arguments": {"frontendOnly": true}, "rows": "data", "match": {"systemName": "{step.categories[item.key].id}"}, "assert": {"kind": "count", "op": "eq", "value": 1}, "source": "skills/dw-pim-modelling/references/model-writes.md"}
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "provenOn": [
    {"dwVersion": "10.30.6", "mcpVersion": "0.6.3-BETA", "date": "2026-11-19", "evidence": "pim.data-models.1-verify.json (all WOULD-CREATE), pim.data-models.2-apply.json (16 of 16 from empty), pim.data-models.3-verify.json and pim.data-models.4-apply-again.json (16 of 16, nothing written), pim.data-models.5-mcponly.json (categories BLOCKED as declared); a hyphenated group key stored its category without the hyphen and was found by name; the catalogue recipe proved the display group on the delivery API and a completeness figure on its products"},
    {"dwVersion": "10.30.6", "mcpVersion": "0.6.6-BETA", "date": "2026-11-19", "evidence": "the whole-build recipe set on a fresh fictional input after the add-in was rolled 0.6.3-BETA -> 0.6.6-BETA (Update-HostAddIn): 1-verify (all eleven recipes WOULD-CREATE), 2-apply, 3-verify (11 of 11 recipes), 4-apply-again (nothing written, no debt owed), 5-verify after a brand restore (11 of 11); the same input then verified 11 of 11 on the add-in rolled back to 0.6.3. 6-mcponly is an MCP-only apply on a second fresh input. This recipe: 15 of 15. On 0.6.6 get_completion_rules rows carry only fieldSystemNames; the read gated on fields[] (requiresSchema) falls to the fieldSystemNames binding, and a separate 0.6.3 run created two rules from empty through the fields[] read-back (15 of 15, apply-again nothing written). MCP-only 1 of 15: the categories have no MCP read, as declared."}
  ],
  "traps": [
    "A top group is one data model and one product category; subgroups carry no spec fields. Data model names must be unique across the PIM shop's folders, because the models are found by name.",
    "On a build whose data models came from a sample-data layer the categories and fields carry the layer's slot ids, so this recipe verifies only a build it applied; check the layer build with the ledger checks.",
    "A product scores completeness only through a rule assigned to a group it sits in: get_completeness_status answers -1 when no rule applies. The catalogue recipe proves the figure on its products."
  ]
}
